---
// The problem → solution narrative.
---
<section class="sec" id="why">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <p class="label-mono sec-eyebrow">// the chore nobody wants to own</p>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Stop babysitting certificates.</h2>
      <p class="sec-lede">
        You terminate public TLS at the edge — but the hop from there to your backends, and traffic
        between internal services, is often plaintext or hand-made certs that expire and page someone
        at 2&nbsp;a.m. syscert makes every host responsible for its own cert, automatically.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="why-split">
      <div class="card why-card why-before">
        <p class="why-tag why-tag-bad">Without syscert</p>
        <ul class="why-list">
          <li>Run an internal CA, then issue + copy + chmod per host</li>
          <li>Cron jobs and shell scripts you hope still work</li>
          <li>Reload nginx by hand; fix SELinux denials later</li>
          <li>A renewal nobody owns → an outage at 2&nbsp;a.m.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="why-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
      <div class="card why-card why-after">
        <p class="why-tag why-tag-good">With syscert</p>
        <ul class="why-list">
          <li>One binary per host; it owns its own certificate</li>
          <li>A <code>systemd</code> timer renews it forever — no cron</li>
          <li>Delivered with the right owner, mode &amp; SELinux context</li>
          <li>Set it once. Walk away. It just stays valid.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .why-split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr; gap: 18px; align-items: center; }
  .why-card { min-width: 0; }
  .why-card { padding: 26px 26px 28px; }
  .why-after { border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--green) 32%, var(--line)); box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in oklab, var(--green) 10%, transparent), 0 24px 60px -44px color-mix(in oklab, var(--green) 60%, transparent); }
  .why-tag { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.06em; margin: 0 0 16px; padding-bottom: 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft); }
  .why-tag-bad { color: var(--faint); }
  .why-tag-good { color: var(--green); }
  .why-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 13px; font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--muted); }
  .why-list li { padding-left: 22px; position: relative; }
  .why-before .why-list li::before { content: "✕"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--faint); }
  .why-after .why-list li::before { content: "✓"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--green); }
  .why-list code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.88em; color: var(--ink); }
  .why-arrow { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 22px; color: var(--faint); }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .why-split { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .why-arrow { rotate: 90deg; justify-self: center; }
  }
</style>
